From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:22:33 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 95/99] Startup shows the shown space's tab; sidebar opens stay
 in their space; no crash on a stale root view
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- At startup (after a crash, say) the window could show a new tab of the
  main space while the sidebar came back on a space of another profile; a
  pinned tab clicked there then followed that tab (its opener) into the
  main space, the sidebar with it. The shown space's tab comes up, and
  only a link's tab joins its opener's space.
- ⌘⌥↑/↓ taken before the page run after the key is handled, not inside
  the page's input handling.
- RenderWidgetHostViewMac::GetRootFrameSinkId() after Destroy(): no
  compositor, no root (a focus change in a tab crashed the browser).
- Test hook: a key through NSApp with the window made key (1 << 30).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
